<h2 id='who-its-for'>🎯 Who Cloudways Is (and Isn't) For</h2>

**Cloudways is the right call if you are:**

A jewelry or watch brand running WooCommerce or Magento with $250K–$10M in annual online GMV. You need server performance that matches the brand experience your customers expect — slow checkout on a $4,000 watch purchase is a conversion killer and a brand trust problem. You want managed infrastructure without a full-time DevOps hire. You run occasional high-traffic events (new collection drops, trunk shows, influencer-driven traffic spikes) that would overwhelm shared hosting.

Cloudways also works well for multi-door luxury retailers who want to run separate WooCommerce instances per brand or per region on the same Cloudways account — you can manage multiple server and application combinations from one dashboard.

**Cloudways is not the right call if you are:**

Running a Shopify store — Cloudways is irrelevant, Shopify handles hosting natively. A single-door boutique doing under $50K online annually — at that revenue level, a well-configured managed WordPress host (Kinsta, WP Engine) may be simpler to operate. A brand that needs a fully white-glove managed service with guaranteed SLAs backed by enterprise support contracts — at that level, look at WP Engine's enterprise tier or Nexcess for Magento.

